You FINALLY managed to sort of get in the right position, but every movement twists a bit and gets you off the desired angle. <<if $muscle < 25>>You try flexing your (mostly nonexistent) muscles, and it frankly just makes you look pathetic.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You tense your still developing muscles - you can tell there’s something there. But just barely. It looks a bit silly, frankly.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>With a flex of your newly-gained muscles, you watch as your arms and chest come to life. It’s not much, but the fruit of your work reminds you of the effort you have put in so far.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>The muscles in your chest and arm come to life, and you surprise yourself at how good your profile looks. And that’s just the beginning, you remind yourself.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>The large bodybuilder looking back at you makes you have a double take, losing your position in the process. But it reassures you that at least your physique is on point.<<else>>You are reminded that you are going to need a bigger mirror, because you have so much beef that only once you get exact posing precision will you be able to fit all of it in that mirror. What you lack in posing experience you more than make it up with muscle.<</if>><br><br> This posing thing will need a lot of work, that much is clear. You promise yourself you will keep at it. But in the meantime, you figure it’s worth doing a bit of testing how strong these muscles you are cultivating are. So what is on the menu today?<br><br> Ah, yes, those apples you got from the grocery store that were kinda disgusting - bitter and mealy. You don’t plan to eat those, so why not find a better use for them in testing your grip strength? You grab one, tossing it to the air and grabbing it back, wrapping your fingers tightly as you start to apply pressure.<br><br> <<if $muscle < 25>>You stare as your hand starts trembling along your entire arm, and you grit your teeth. With a grunt, you give up and toss the apple back in the basket. You win today, fruit. But just you wait...<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You do your best to squeeze, and you feel the hardness of the apple being surprisingly resilient. Yet, your fingertips get some purchase - you are not sure if it’s your nails or your muscle, but you get to break the skin a bit. You give up, watching at the apple with some dents at the top, and lick your lips, fantasizing about the day you will be able to utterly obliterate that red foe.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You put all of your effort into squeezing the fruit, which makes a weird squelching noise as the juice starts running down your wrist and forearm. You leave an imprint of your fingers on the apple, which you admire as some sort of bizarre sculpture. You’d frame it if it wouldn’t spoil, so you give it a bite before remembering how awful it tastes, and tossing it into the trash - hopefully, the next one will be able to go down the drain.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You confidently squeeze the apple, which trembles under your fingertips. A smile starts spreading through your face as you feel its structure giving in. You grit your teeth and redouble your efforts, and the fruit slowly collapses into three chunks under your hand. You watch the shattered plant as you toss its remains in the bin. But you are not satisfied until you actually juice that damn thing effortlessly.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You grab the apple with a knowing smile. You squeeze, and while there is some resistance initially, you give it a tighter squeeze and the fruit quickly gives, collapsing into bits with a delicious CRUNCH. You watch the bits of fruit in your wet palm, before tossing the parts in the trash and wiping your hands. You open and close your hand, happy… but not completely satisfied. You know there’s still some room for improvement, and giggle maliciously with what’s yet to come.<<else>>You grab the apple and just hold it idly on your open palm. An evil grin forms in your face. It’s time for the foul fruit to pay.<br><br> Your fingers close and squeeze, and the apple easily liquifies under your fingertips - leaving no more than a mushed paste. And you barely even put any effort. Is it time to graduate into crushing rocks, you ask yourself, as you take pride in your hard-earned might.<</if>>
	<<elseif _posingLevel is 1>>
