	The bedroom feels strangely silent as you face the mirror. You start undressing for your posing practice, pretending like the mirror is your audience at the big show. <<if $muscle < 25>>You briefly wonder the point of exposing your muscleless body, but it’s still going to help to understand the mechanics of your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You are briefly reminded of your progress as you notice your toned body, but right now, there’s still a lot of work to be done on your physique.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your burgeoning musculature is unwrapped like a present, revealing your hard gained (and equally hard to the touch) muscles, which you are about to put to work.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your impressive muscles come to life from under the fabric, ready to come into the limelight.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You feel the excitement as your physique is revealed, confirming that all the hard work you have put has paid off, as you watch some of the biggest muscles you ever laid eyes on come out of their fabric cage.<<else>>It’s actually a bit awkward to even unrobe the massive mountains of sinew, but your gigantic body makes you giggle with delight as you prepare to put them on display.<</if>> Feeling somewhat brave, you decide to go for a most muscular pose, which feels like the proper way to mog with your musculature.<br><br> Taking a step back, you lean forward and kind of just haphazardly try to flex your entire upper body - and it’s a bit of a disaster. <<if $muscle < 25>>Frankly, even if you were doing it right, what would be the point? Right now, you don’t put the \‘muscular\’ in \‘most muscular\’.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>It’s nice to see that you have SOMETHING to flex… but the actual flexing leaves quite a lot to be desired, and you are not even sure what you are doing wrong.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You manage to get some muscle out of your arms, but looking at your shoulders it’s painfully obvious you need to train how to pop your traps, as the pose looks quite underwhelming.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You get your arms to flare, but it frustrates you how little action you are getting on your shoulders and traps, as the added volume makes your top half kind of pathetic.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Your muscular arms sure steal the show, but that just makes the glaring observation that you do not know how to engage your traps and shoulders clear, and it feels like a bucket of cold water on your posing.<<else>>Your larger than life upper arms somehow explode in width from their already respectable size… but as you look at yourself in the mirror, you notice that your upper body somehow feels wrong - there’s no action along your neck and shoulders, reminding you that there’s quite a bit of training you will need to land this pose.<</if>> You repeat the process a few times, with no further success. And with a sigh and a slump of your very unflexed deltoids, you know that your posing needs a lot of work still.<br><br> But not all hope is lost. These muscles may not be for show, but they might still be up for a small show of strength. And as such, you decide to go for the exposed pipes in the maintenance area and see what’s up with your ability to hang and lift yourself.<br><br> You find one of reinforced metal pipes, jumping towards it so your fingers can wrap around it. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your grip almost slip as it’s just barely able to sustain your body. You feel your puny shoulders stretching as your arms try their hardest to keep you from falling, but it quickly becomes clear you need to foster your strength a lot more… it’s barely a few seconds before your back, arms and fingers fail, making you awkwardly fall back to the ground. Thankfully, this was not a movie-like situation where you life depended on it, but you feel the drive to improve your strength as much as your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Your hands manage to hold on firmly to the pipe, your grip quite able to secure you hanging from it. Your shoulders and back, however, quickly start feeling the strain. But you endure, timing your effort to see how long you can hold on. You grit your teeth, trying your hardest to make sure you can do it for at least 30 seconds. You can feel the burn as you reach the mark, dropping with exhausted but proud muscles. You are quite determined to get that time increased.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your strong legs easily give you the boost to comfortably grasp the pipe, and your equally strong hands hold on tightly to the pipe. You don’t feel nearly as anxious as your body courageously holds on for 15… 30… 45 seconds. At the minute mark, you start feeling the burn, so you hold on as long as you can, but already feeling accomplished on your newfound strength. Perhaps you should start making the exercise harder….<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You confidently jump towards the pipe, which despite being quite thick and stable with several bracers, shakes from your considerable mass. Still, your strength is such that hanging feels a bit futile, so you decide to make it more interesting, bending your elbows at ninety degrees. Your biceps round themselves out at as you hold midway through a chin up, with big upper arms bringing a smile to your lips. You feel the sinewy muscles of your upper body engaging, and behold how large it has become. Time passes, and you surprise yourself with being able to hold in this position for so long. Perhaps soon it will be time to take things up a notch.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You jump back to the pipe, this time holding on with one hand, bent at the elbow. Your arms inflate dramatically, and you can only assume your back must look amazing - making you wish there was a couple of mirrors there. Still, you feel somewhat superhuman as you hold with a single-hand grip for several seconds. It’s getting harder to believe just how strong you are getting as you dismount.<<else>>Feeling like it’s time to really push this to the limit, you hold yourself with one hand, and start cranking chin-ups. You amaze yourself at your ability to just lift yourself with one arm, knowing full well that you have also grown CONSIDERABLY heavier since you started. It’s actually sort of mind blowing. And when you let go, you notice that your fingers actually left marks on the steel pipe. Did you just bend it… with your fingertips? That is going to take some time to process…<</if>><br><br> Back on the ground, you stretch your shoulders as you return to your apartment, looking forward to your next training session.
	<<elseif _posingLevel is 1>>
	The bedroom feels strangely silent as you face the mirror. You start undressing for your posing practice, pretending like the mirror is your audience at the big show. <<if $muscle < 25>>You briefly wonder the point of exposing your muscleless body, but it’s still going to help to understand the mechanics of your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You are briefly reminded of your progress as you notice your toned body, but right now, there’s still a lot of work to be done on your physique.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your burgeoning musculature is unwrapped like a present, revealing your hard gained (and equally hard to the touch) muscles, which you are about to put to work.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your impressive muscles come to life from under the fabric, ready to come into the limelight.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You feel the excitement as your physique is revealed, confirming that all the hard work you have put has paid off, as you watch some of the biggest muscles you ever laid eyes on come out of their fabric cage.<<else>>It’s actually a bit awkward to even unrobe the massive mountains of sinew, but your gigantic body makes you giggle with delight as you prepare to put them on display.<</if>> Feeling somewhat brave, you decide to go for a most muscular pose, which feels like the proper way to mog with your musculature.<br><br> Feeling a bit more confident, you step away from the mirror, lean forward and just squeeze all these muscles, watching for your figure to change with the move. <<if $muscle < 25>>You are still disappointed with your puny muscles, but at least now you managed to sort of engage your traps - or where they would be, if you had any. Well, more reason to keep working on it.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You almost gasp as you watch SOMETHING popping around your neck, as you somehow get your traps to engage. There’s some shoulder action as well, but you are clearly not quite there yet.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Two mounds rise next to your neck, making you feel like some sort of comic book character - which is a bit generous of you, but still, progress IS progress. But now you notice your shoulders fail to engage in the same fashion, giving you an uneven look. You try rolling them awkwardly, to no avail..<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You watch incredulously as your neck is surrounded by two respectable mountains of muscle, making you feel incredibly strong and thick. But your eyes soon wander towards your shoulders, and your deltoids apparently never got an invitation to the party. You move and twist trying to fix that, but it’s no use. You will need more training.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>And just like that, your neck is suddenly buried by two peaks of sinew, which tells you why this pose gets its name. Except your shoulders ruin the effect, failing to flex with the same ferocity. You try your hardest, but you will need more experience before this works.<<else>>Your large figure is already straining the mirror, but then your traps just jumpscare the hell out of you, as if you are literally undergoing some crazy superhero transformation. The difference is stark and impressive - but quite disappointing as you realize that your capped shoulders never accompany the rest of the expansion, which feels very wrong. You just know you can make those footballs into CANNON balls - but that will take some more effort.<</if>> You can tell you had some progress in your posing, but the road ahead still feel quite long.<br><br> Still, you feel like you are getting somewhere. And perhaps now you could see what these muscles can do. And as such, you decide to go for the exposed pipes in the maintenance area and see what’s up with your ability to hang and lift yourself.<br><br> You find one of reinforced metal pipes, jumping towards it so your fingers can wrap around it. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your grip almost slip as it’s just barely able to sustain your body. You feel your puny shoulders stretching as your arms try their hardest to keep you from falling, but it quickly becomes clear you need to foster your strength a lot more… it’s barely a few seconds before your back, arms and fingers fail, making you awkwardly fall back to the ground. Thankfully, this was not a movie-like situation where you life depended on it, but you feel the drive to improve your strength as much as your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Your hands manage to hold on firmly to the pipe, your grip quite able to secure you hanging from it. Your shoulders and back, however, quickly start feeling the strain. But you endure, timing your effort to see how long you can hold on. You grit your teeth, trying your hardest to make sure you can do it for at least 30 seconds. You can feel the burn as you reach the mark, dropping with exhausted but proud muscles. You are quite determined to get that time increased.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your strong legs easily give you the boost to comfortably grasp the pipe, and your equally strong hands hold on tightly to the pipe. You don’t feel nearly as anxious as your body courageously holds on for 15… 30… 45 seconds. At the minute mark, you start feeling the burn, so you hold on as long as you can, but already feeling accomplished on your newfound strength. Perhaps you should start making the exercise harder….<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You confidently jump towards the pipe, which despite being quite thick and stable with several bracers, shakes from your considerable mass. Still, your strength is such that hanging feels a bit futile, so you decide to make it more interesting, bending your elbows at ninety degrees. Your biceps round themselves out at as you hold midway through a chin up, with big upper arms bringing a smile to your lips. You feel the sinewy muscles of your upper body engaging, and behold how large it has become. Time passes, and you surprise yourself with being able to hold in this position for so long. Perhaps soon it will be time to take things up a notch.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You jump back to the pipe, this time holding on with one hand, bent at the elbow. Your arms inflate dramatically, and you can only assume your back must look amazing - making you wish there was a couple of mirrors there. Still, you feel somewhat superhuman as you hold with a single-hand grip for several seconds. It’s getting harder to believe just how strong you are getting as you dismount.<<else>>Feeling like it’s time to really push this to the limit, you hold yourself with one hand, and start cranking chin-ups. You amaze yourself at your ability to just lift yourself with one arm, knowing full well that you have also grown CONSIDERABLY heavier since you started. It’s actually sort of mind blowing. And when you let go, you notice that your fingers actually left marks on the steel pipe. Did you just bend it… with your fingertips? That is going to take some time to process…<</if>><br><br> Back on the ground, you stretch your shoulders as you return to your apartment, looking forward to your next training session.
	<<elseif _posingLevel is 2>>
	The bedroom feels strangely silent as you face the mirror. You start undressing for your posing practice, pretending like the mirror is your audience at the big show. <<if $muscle < 25>>You briefly wonder the point of exposing your muscleless body, but it’s still going to help to understand the mechanics of your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You are briefly reminded of your progress as you notice your toned body, but right now, there’s still a lot of work to be done on your physique.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your burgeoning musculature is unwrapped like a present, revealing your hard gained (and equally hard to the touch) muscles, which you are about to put to work.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your impressive muscles come to life from under the fabric, ready to come into the limelight.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You feel the excitement as your physique is revealed, confirming that all the hard work you have put has paid off, as you watch some of the biggest muscles you ever laid eyes on come out of their fabric cage.<<else>>It’s actually a bit awkward to even unrobe the massive mountains of sinew, but your gigantic body makes you giggle with delight as you prepare to put them on display.<</if>> Feeling somewhat brave, you decide to go for a most muscular pose, which feels like the proper way to mog with your musculature.<br><br> Without thinking, you take a step back and lean forward with your arms, letting out a small grunt as you flex. <<if $muscle < 25>>It sounds a bit stupid, as your face goes red but your body refuses to show any clear musculature. But at least now you feel like you engaged all nearly-nonexistent muscles on the topmost part of your torso.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>With relief, you watch your shoulders join in on the fun with your traps, giving you quite a wide appearance. But now your attention is drawn to your chest, which you didn’t give as much attention, and it shows.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your traps and shoulders fill you with the same delight your arms did, making you look incredibly wide and defined, rounded shapes screaming THICK!. However, you now notice that you failed to do the same with your pectorals, and it’s sad because you KNOW they can look quite rugged. But you aren’t quite there yet.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your shoulders explode into capped onions, looking very sinewy and bumpy, giving you that great wide look. What ISN’T, though, is your chest, which you trained enough to know it can look just as muscular. But no matter how much you try, you fail in bringing it out.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>True cannonballs materialize on the base of your arms, which go hand in hand with your incredible traps and just make you look downright scary strong. But your happiness doesn’t last long as you can’t seem to flex your pectoral muscles while keeping this top part engaged, and it frustrates you endlessly, confirming you need more practice.<<else>>Your impossible physique explodes around your head as the muscles make it look tiny around your traps and delts. The effect is actually a bit jarring, to the point where it feels like your head shrank in the process. But your excitement doesn’t last long as you notice your chest failed to join on the ride. You’ve seen your pectorals swell and display incredibly strong ridges, but it’s not happening right now, no matter how hard you try.<</if>> You repeat the process a few times, but only more practice will fix it. So you decide to focus on your front going forward, but at least you feel like you’ve made some real progress.<br><br> Eager to get that physique engaged in more practical matters, you switch your focus. And thus, you decide to go for the exposed pipes in the maintenance area and see what’s up with your ability to hang and lift yourself.<br><br> You find one of reinforced metal pipes, jumping towards it so your fingers can wrap around it. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your grip almost slip as it’s just barely able to sustain your body. You feel your puny shoulders stretching as your arms try their hardest to keep you from falling, but it quickly becomes clear you need to foster your strength a lot more… it’s barely a few seconds before your back, arms and fingers fail, making you awkwardly fall back to the ground. Thankfully, this was not a movie-like situation where you life depended on it, but you feel the drive to improve your strength as much as your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Your hands manage to hold on firmly to the pipe, your grip quite able to secure you hanging from it. Your shoulders and back, however, quickly start feeling the strain. But you endure, timing your effort to see how long you can hold on. You grit your teeth, trying your hardest to make sure you can do it for at least 30 seconds. You can feel the burn as you reach the mark, dropping with exhausted but proud muscles. You are quite determined to get that time increased.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your strong legs easily give you the boost to comfortably grasp the pipe, and your equally strong hands hold on tightly to the pipe. You don’t feel nearly as anxious as your body courageously holds on for 15… 30… 45 seconds. At the minute mark, you start feeling the burn, so you hold on as long as you can, but already feeling accomplished on your newfound strength. Perhaps you should start making the exercise harder….<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You confidently jump towards the pipe, which despite being quite thick and stable with several bracers, shakes from your considerable mass. Still, your strength is such that hanging feels a bit futile, so you decide to make it more interesting, bending your elbows at ninety degrees. Your biceps round themselves out at as you hold midway through a chin up, with big upper arms bringing a smile to your lips. You feel the sinewy muscles of your upper body engaging, and behold how large it has become. Time passes, and you surprise yourself with being able to hold in this position for so long. Perhaps soon it will be time to take things up a notch.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You jump back to the pipe, this time holding on with one hand, bent at the elbow. Your arms inflate dramatically, and you can only assume your back must look amazing - making you wish there was a couple of mirrors there. Still, you feel somewhat superhuman as you hold with a single-hand grip for several seconds. It’s getting harder to believe just how strong you are getting as you dismount.<<else>>Feeling like it’s time to really push this to the limit, you hold yourself with one hand, and start cranking chin-ups. You amaze yourself at your ability to just lift yourself with one arm, knowing full well that you have also grown CONSIDERABLY heavier since you started. It’s actually sort of mind blowing. And when you let go, you notice that your fingers actually left marks on the steel pipe. Did you just bend it… with your fingertips? That is going to take some time to process…<</if>><br><br> Back on the ground, you stretch your shoulders as you return to your apartment, looking forward to your next training session.
	<<elseif _posingLevel is 3>>
	The bedroom feels strangely silent as you face the mirror. You start undressing for your posing practice, pretending like the mirror is your audience at the big show. <<if $muscle < 25>>You briefly wonder the point of exposing your muscleless body, but it’s still going to help to understand the mechanics of your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You are briefly reminded of your progress as you notice your toned body, but right now, there’s still a lot of work to be done on your physique.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your burgeoning musculature is unwrapped like a present, revealing your hard gained (and equally hard to the touch) muscles, which you are about to put to work.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your impressive muscles come to life from under the fabric, ready to come into the limelight.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You feel the excitement as your physique is revealed, confirming that all the hard work you have put has paid off, as you watch some of the biggest muscles you ever laid eyes on come out of their fabric cage.<<else>>It’s actually a bit awkward to even unrobe the massive mountains of sinew, but your gigantic body makes you giggle with delight as you prepare to put them on display.<</if>> Feeling somewhat brave, you decide to go for a most muscular pose, which feels like the proper way to mog with your musculature.<br><br> Putting your practice to use, you take your usual position in front of the mirror and just FLEX! <<if $muscle < 25>>Boom! You can feel the muscles engaging… you just really can’t see much. It kinda feels you nailed most of the pose, even if there is no muscle to impress anyone. And to make matters worse, your legs kinda make you look like you need to go to the bathroom. You are going to need to work on that next.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Wow, it really feels like some actual progress - your mass might still be humble, but you somehow make the most of it and your entire upper body sings in unison, giving you quite a powerful - if a bit modest - figure. But now looking more generally at the mirror, you notice your legs are all awkward as you lean forward, keeping you from looking really confident. You will have to work on that before going onstage for real.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You watch the magic happen as your entire upper body engorges with beautiful sinew, every bit pumped and rounded out with marvelous muscle. You feel the widest you’ve ever been, able to tell each muscle apart with ease. It’s exhilarating… but… your legs. With all the leaning forward, you notice you are standing quite awkwardly, and it takes away from the total accomplishment.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You can barely believe your eyes as you watch what can only be described as a true bodybuilder, large bumps and ridges in every tiny part of your upper body. You feel wide, strong and powerful. That is, until you look at your legs, which you ignored so far - and now realize are in a very weird position that sort of throws off the /’I am woman, hear me roar/’ thing you had going.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Muscles upon muscles explode all over your torso, as your neck, shoulders, arms and chest all strain and expand, revealing a powerful figure that is impossible to ignore. Your jaw drops as you realize that is very much yourself on the mirror, looking like the biggest of bodybuilders. But for all the confidence it gives you, your lower body looks kind of pathetic as you neglected to properly position your legs this entire time. And every time you try to adjust them, you flub something else. Oh, well.<<else>>Words fail you as a literal mountain range of muscles surges from your waist to your neck, every little bit of your body looking like a monstrous pile of impossible, veiny muscle. Ridiculous traps, deltoids that would make cannonballs blush. A chest so ridged one could crack nuts between your pectorals. Arms that look like they could break metal chains. You are the very incarnation of power… but the illusion is kind of broken by your legs, which feel like they don’t know quite where to go and give you a very lopsided appearance.<</if>> While it’s kind of frustrating to be so close to a perfect pose, it feels like it won’t take much to make it perfect. This will be more than worth it, you tell yourself.<br><br> Encouraged by your progress, you decide to put your muscles to task. And as such, you go for the exposed pipes in the maintenance area and see what’s up with your ability to hang and lift yourself.<br><br> You find one of reinforced metal pipes, jumping towards it so your fingers can wrap around it. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your grip almost slip as it’s just barely able to sustain your body. You feel your puny shoulders stretching as your arms try their hardest to keep you from falling, but it quickly becomes clear you need to foster your strength a lot more… it’s barely a few seconds before your back, arms and fingers fail, making you awkwardly fall back to the ground. Thankfully, this was not a movie-like situation where you life depended on it, but you feel the drive to improve your strength as much as your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Your hands manage to hold on firmly to the pipe, your grip quite able to secure you hanging from it. Your shoulders and back, however, quickly start feeling the strain. But you endure, timing your effort to see how long you can hold on. You grit your teeth, trying your hardest to make sure you can do it for at least 30 seconds. You can feel the burn as you reach the mark, dropping with exhausted but proud muscles. You are quite determined to get that time increased.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your strong legs easily give you the boost to comfortably grasp the pipe, and your equally strong hands hold on tightly to the pipe. You don’t feel nearly as anxious as your body courageously holds on for 15… 30… 45 seconds. At the minute mark, you start feeling the burn, so you hold on as long as you can, but already feeling accomplished on your newfound strength. Perhaps you should start making the exercise harder….<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You confidently jump towards the pipe, which despite being quite thick and stable with several bracers, shakes from your considerable mass. Still, your strength is such that hanging feels a bit futile, so you decide to make it more interesting, bending your elbows at ninety degrees. Your biceps round themselves out at as you hold midway through a chin up, with big upper arms bringing a smile to your lips. You feel the sinewy muscles of your upper body engaging, and behold how large it has become. Time passes, and you surprise yourself with being able to hold in this position for so long. Perhaps soon it will be time to take things up a notch.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You jump back to the pipe, this time holding on with one hand, bent at the elbow. Your arms inflate dramatically, and you can only assume your back must look amazing - making you wish there was a couple of mirrors there. Still, you feel somewhat superhuman as you hold with a single-hand grip for several seconds. It’s getting harder to believe just how strong you are getting as you dismount.<<else>>Feeling like it’s time to really push this to the limit, you hold yourself with one hand, and start cranking chin-ups. You amaze yourself at your ability to just lift yourself with one arm, knowing full well that you have also grown CONSIDERABLY heavier since you started. It’s actually sort of mind blowing. And when you let go, you notice that your fingers actually left marks on the steel pipe. Did you just bend it… with your fingertips? That is going to take some time to process…<</if>><br><br> Back on the ground, you stretch your shoulders as you return to your apartment, looking forward to your next training session.
	<<else>>
	The bedroom feels strangely silent as you face the mirror. You start undressing for your posing practice, pretending like the mirror is your audience at the big show. <<if $muscle < 25>>You briefly wonder the point of exposing your muscleless body, but it’s still going to help to understand the mechanics of your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>You are briefly reminded of your progress as you notice your toned body, but right now, there’s still a lot of work to be done on your physique.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your burgeoning musculature is unwrapped like a present, revealing your hard gained (and equally hard to the touch) muscles, which you are about to put to work.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your impressive muscles come to life from under the fabric, ready to come into the limelight.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You feel the excitement as your physique is revealed, confirming that all the hard work you have put has paid off, as you watch some of the biggest muscles you ever laid eyes on come out of their fabric cage.<<else>>It’s actually a bit awkward to even unrobe the massive mountains of sinew, but your gigantic body makes you giggle with delight as you prepare to put them on display.<</if>> Feeling somewhat brave, you decide to go for a most muscular pose, which feels like the proper way to mog with your musculature.<br><br> Almost instinctively, you close your eyes as you step away from the mirror. You just flex. When you open your eyes, you can barely believe them. <<if $muscle < 25>>Sure, you’d still be humbled onstage because of your physique… but you simply NAILED the pose.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>That’s it. The perfect most muscular pose. It could use some… well… muscles. But it’s clear you are making the most of what mass you gained, as your body displays some decent bumps all around your upper body.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You are amazed to see what proper posing can do. Sure, your musculature is just above average - but you look downright intimidating in that pose, your torso looking wide and powerful.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>It’s like you are looking at some idealized superheroine on the mirror. You marvel at your own gains as your traps, shoulders, chest, arms and abs seem like they were taken from an anatomy book. You giggle with excitement at your progress.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>What you see could easily be on the cover of a superhero comic, an idealized body that would not look bad on a male hero - let alone a female one. Right now, you feel like you could lift a car, that’s how impressive you look.<<else>>...<br><br>...<br><br>You can barely articulate what you see. The strongest, most powerful and intimidating human to ever have walked this Earth, a true Atlas, capable of carrying the world on her back. It truly is a titanic presence, with traps the size of bricks, deltoids the size of large beachballs, biceps the size of watermelons, pectorals larger than cantaloupes. Just how strong you actually are is hard to even fathom.<</if>> You know for a fact that you are now one step closer to winning that bodybuilding contest.<br><br> With that issue of posing now firmly behind you, you feel like you should take these muscles for a spin with a small test of strength. And as such, you decide to go for the exposed pipes in the maintenance area and see what’s up with your ability to hang and lift yourself.<br><br> You find one of reinforced metal pipes, jumping towards it so your fingers can wrap around it. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your grip almost slip as it’s just barely able to sustain your body. You feel your puny shoulders stretching as your arms try their hardest to keep you from falling, but it quickly becomes clear you need to foster your strength a lot more… it’s barely a few seconds before your back, arms and fingers fail, making you awkwardly fall back to the ground. Thankfully, this was not a movie-like situation where you life depended on it, but you feel the drive to improve your strength as much as your posing.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Your hands manage to hold on firmly to the pipe, your grip quite able to secure you hanging from it. Your shoulders and back, however, quickly start feeling the strain. But you endure, timing your effort to see how long you can hold on. You grit your teeth, trying your hardest to make sure you can do it for at least 30 seconds. You can feel the burn as you reach the mark, dropping with exhausted but proud muscles. You are quite determined to get that time increased.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your strong legs easily give you the boost to comfortably grasp the pipe, and your equally strong hands hold on tightly to the pipe. You don’t feel nearly as anxious as your body courageously holds on for 15… 30… 45 seconds. At the minute mark, you start feeling the burn, so you hold on as long as you can, but already feeling accomplished on your newfound strength. Perhaps you should start making the exercise harder….<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You confidently jump towards the pipe, which despite being quite thick and stable with several bracers, shakes from your considerable mass. Still, your strength is such that hanging feels a bit futile, so you decide to make it more interesting, bending your elbows at ninety degrees. Your biceps round themselves out at as you hold midway through a chin up, with big upper arms bringing a smile to your lips. You feel the sinewy muscles of your upper body engaging, and behold how large it has become. Time passes, and you surprise yourself with being able to hold in this position for so long. Perhaps soon it will be time to take things up a notch.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You jump back to the pipe, this time holding on with one hand, bent at the elbow. Your arms inflate dramatically, and you can only assume your back must look amazing - making you wish there was a couple of mirrors there. Still, you feel somewhat superhuman as you hold with a single-hand grip for several seconds. It’s getting harder to believe just how strong you are getting as you dismount.<<else>>Feeling like it’s time to really push this to the limit, you hold yourself with one hand, and start cranking chin-ups. You amaze yourself at your ability to just lift yourself with one arm, knowing full well that you have also grown CONSIDERABLY heavier since you started. It’s actually sort of mind blowing. And when you let go, you notice that your fingers actually left marks on the steel pipe. Did you just bend it… with your fingertips? That is going to take some time to process…<</if>><br><br> Back on the ground, you stretch your shoulders as you return to your apartment, looking forward to your next training session.
