shoulders wide and waist comparatively small. It’s almost intoxicating to realize all you have accomplished.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>With the musculature of a proper bodybuilder, you now have the posing to match, making your back look downright impressive: wide, ridged and cutting a mean taper.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>With muscles that would not look bad on a male bodybuilder, you finally manage to engage the lat spread well enough that no one would ever guess you weren’t a professional in the sport for years.<<else>>The almost literal mountains you call your back erupt under your command, as you widen with each second. Except now they settle, decided, imponent. Impossible to ignore. And impossible to ignore.<</if>> You feel so close to literal perfection. It’s certainly good enough, but you are sure there’s still a little room for improvement.<br><br> Feeling accomplished, you decide to try something to measure what these muscles of yours can actually do. And so you throw yourself into your attempt at a planche, that one exercise where you hold yourself off the ground with just your hands. You try to remember the guides you saw earlier, and it seemed quite daunting, but with training and conditioning, you decide to keep your hopes up. <<if $muscle < 25>>You put your hands on the ground, but even a basic push up is proving to be a bit challenging. You come to the realization it’s going to be a long road...<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Feeling a bit more confident, you decide to try a planche tuck, just lifting yourself with your legs bent in front of your chest. It might not look like the easiest move, but the reality is somehow even more daunting. You sort of get into the position, but just barely. You clearly need to work on your muscles a bit more before you can take this any further.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You go for the planche tuck, and actually manage to hit the pose, holding it for what you believe is a good 10-15 seconds, though it feels like an eternity. It inspires you to keep at it, maybe soon you will get to your goal.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You go for a planche tuck, which proves to be pretty manageable as you get to a nice half-minute in that position. So you go that next step and try a piked straddle planche, raising your hips and opening your legs to the sides. It’s not the easiest, but you manage. And so you try to see how long you can hold that pose until you move to the real deal.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You finally manage to pull a very consistent piked straddle planche, so with bated breath, you go to the real deal. You slowly stretch your legs back, feeling the tension spread through your body. You tremble, trying to get that proper balance so you don’t fall. Seconds feel like years as your legs come together and finally… FINALLY… stretch all the way into a proper planche. You maintain the pose for a couple of seconds, still shaking, before settling back down.<<else>>Placing your hands firmly to support yourself, you calmly start engaging your core and legs in a proper planche. It’s not easy, but it’s also not hard. You stand… or rather, lie straight… proud of your incredible feat of strength, knowing the power you hold within this incredible body.<</if>> And so you get back up, and continue with your day.
	<<else>>
	You return to the mirror, thinking about the necessary practice for a bodybuilding competition. Best way to learn how to pose is practice, right? So you start taking your outerwear in order to see if you can nail a proper lat spread. <<if $muscle < 25>>You see your shoulder blades and confuse them for muscle for a second, getting a bit disappointed.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Your back looks quite bare, with little muscle or volume to be seen.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Your work is starting to pay off, as you see some bumps on your back, leading you to change to an overhead light to maximize the effect.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your back is looking quite strong already, feeling broader and bumpier, which makes you giddy.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You impress yourself with your gains, watching a wide and muscular back of your torso by twisting your neck to the mirror.<<else>>You have to use your phone’s camera as an improvised mirror to truly appreciate the gigantic back muscles you developed on the mirror, inspiring you to make some social media poses as you are awed with the impressive physique being exhibited.<</if>> With the goods on full display, you start trying to do a proper lat spread.<br><br> With not a single iota of hesitation, you just plant your hands on your hips and flex. <<if $muscle < 25>>You might not have muscle, but you have confidence and presence. Anyone would stop and watch - even if they were a bit confused by such a wimpy wannabe bodybuilder.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>If the mirror was alive, it would stop everything it was doing to stare. Your small gains are put on impeccable display that would leave most seasoned bodybuilders impressed - if not for your physique, for your perfectly executed pose.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You make every bit of your gains count as an indisputably perfect lat spread is executed, making your shoulders look enormous and in contrast with a narrowing waist. It’s inspiring - not only for the enviable posing, but because it makes you thirst for more muscle, dreaming of how amazing this would look with a proper bodybuilder physique.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>There is no doubt that you made it: huge muscles are put on the most perfect display of a lat spread you’ve ever seen… and probably any competitor, really. You have no doubt this competition is in the bag already… except… deep inside, you KNOW you can get bigger. Stronger. It almost makes you salivate as you fantasize about getting impossibly big and flaunting this hard-earned posing skills.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Massive. There’s no other word to describe what your enviable mass and your perfected posing accomplish together. You feel like you could easily dominate every single competitor, male or female, in this competition. Makes you anxious for the actual show.<<else>>Speechless. That is how you are left as impossible muscles encounter incomparable posing of a lat spread. You’ve heard of the infamous Christmas Tree - but you are more like the entire forest right now, an undeniable force of nature taken to the utmost level of perfection. Huge. Confident. POWERFUL.<</if>> There is no question: there is no point in trying to improve your posing - it’s simply peak.<br><br> With nothing more to accomplish on the actual training for the perfect lat spread, you decide all you have left is to bring the actual muscles to a test of their strength. And so you prepare to accomplish just that with a planche, that one exercise where you hold yourself off the ground with just your hands. You try to remember the guides you saw earlier, and it seemed quite daunting, but with training and conditioning, you decide to keep your hopes up. <<if $muscle < 25>>You put your hands on the ground, but even a basic push up is proving to be a bit challenging. You come to the realization it’s going to be a long road...<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Feeling a bit more confident, you decide to try a planche tuck, just lifting yourself with your legs bent in front of your chest. It might not look like the easiest move, but the reality is somehow even more daunting. You sort of get into the position, but just barely. You clearly need to work on your muscles a bit more before you can take this any further.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You go for the planche tuck, and actually manage to hit the pose, holding it for what you believe is a good 10-15 seconds, though it feels like an eternity. It inspires you to keep at it, maybe soon you will get to your goal.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You go for a planche tuck, which proves to be pretty manageable as you get to a nice half-minute in that position. So you go that next step and try a piked straddle planche, raising your hips and opening your legs to the sides. It’s not the easiest, but you manage. And so you try to see how long you can hold that pose until you move to the real deal.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You finally manage to pull a very consistent piked straddle planche, so with bated breath, you go to the real deal. You slowly stretch your legs back, feeling the tension spread through your body. You tremble, trying to get that proper balance so you don’t fall. Seconds feel like years as your legs come together and finally… FINALLY… stretch all the way into a proper planche. You maintain the pose for a couple of seconds, still shaking, before settling back down.<<else>>Placing your hands firmly to support yourself, you calmly start engaging your core and legs in a proper planche. It’s not easy, but it’s also not hard. You stand… or rather, lie straight… proud of your incredible feat of strength, knowing the power you hold within this incredible body.<</if>> And so you get back up, and continue with your day.
	<</if>>
<<elseif _posePart is "frontDoubleBiceps">>
	<<if _posingLevel is 0>>
	You stretch in front of the mirror, and get that itch to check how your posing is going, and get some practice in. Rotating your shoulders, you think it’s time to pull out the big guns, figuratively, as you take your top off to try that front double biceps routine. <<if $muscle < 25>>You will have to settle with your twig arms for now, but that just means there’s more room for improvement. <<elseif $muscle < 35>>You want to take these baby guns out for a ride.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You’ve caught yourself plenty of times checking out your own upper arms, so it’s the perfect opportunity.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Given how much people ask to check out your guns, it just feels right.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Not that you even need to flex in order for people to see how thick your arms have become.<<else>>Given that your biceps are already the size of melons even relaxed, this ought to be good.<</if>> You raise your arms tentatively, after all, flexing your biceps is one of the most culturally celebrated displays of strength - how much training could it possibly require?<br><br> As it turns out, more than you expected. <<if $muscle < 25>>You bend your elbows, squeezing with all your might, but no matter what you do, there is no movement to be seen. You keep moving and squeezing harder, expecting to see at least a little bump, but it’s for naught.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>The nascent bumps on your arms dance around, making it clear why the Latin origin of the word muscle comes from “little mouse”: the imaginary rodent wanders up and down your upper arm as you bend your elbow and twist your fist.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You can’t get enough of your pipes, with your newly-acquired biceps making themselves known as your squeeze your arms around.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You almost can’t believe your eyes as your upper arms come to life, and powerful biceps make themselves known and impossible to ignore.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>You marvel at your arms, which already scream BODYBUILDER with their incredible mass and definition. They are one of the more obvious reminders of your progress, catching everyone’s eyes during your daily life as it is.<<else>>You almost forgot the inhuman cannonballs hiding under the skin of your arms as giant mountains erupt, in what can barely be described as “unbelievably huge”.<</if>> But one thing is clear: you have no clue what you are doing. You are pretty sure there are better ways to engage and display your muscles - if only you knew the correct pose and the entire routine to slowly show off what you have. But more practice is necessary at this point.<br><br> But one cannot do a gun show and not want to show off their strength, and so you get all pumped up (heh) for a little test of your strength. You are then reminded that the landlord installed one of those punching arcade games in the landry, what best way to see how powerful you are than with the speed of your fists?<br><br> You arrive at the empty laundry room, the red tower with a punching bag blinking in silence. You gather some pocket change and get in position, trying to channel all those boxing movies you watched - which, incidentally, reminds you that you have no clue what you are doing. And after inserting the coin, the bag is dropped to its lowered position and the machine starts playing some beepy music. Your eyes lock in on your target, and you wind up, preparing to hit your new inanimate foe. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your hand flies and connects with the bag… with a pitiful whimper as it retracts, and the machine barely registers it, showing a 15 out of 999. You secretly hope there is no low score memory, because you feel embarrassed enough as it is.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>The punch hits with a decent thud, and the three digital numbers start rolling as the machine evaluates your punch. It finally settles on a 70 out of 999, which you somehow hope isn’t as low as it sounds. But you notice the high scores in the 350-450 range, and realize you still got some work ahead of you.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Feeling confident, you pretend to dodge a few imaginary punches before letting your fist fly - it lands with a satisfying thump, and you hear the bag recoiling in its housing as the numbers roll… and give you a 275. Not bad, you are getting closer to the high scores in the 350-450 range. You squeeze your fist, looking at the machine, anxious to get yourself in that scoreboard.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You twist your torso, using all your newfound strength and hit the bag with a loud thud, and it flies back into the slot, causing the digital display to come to life… giving you a 390 out of 999, putting you at the middle of the high score list. You pump your fist with excitement, feeling a sudden urge to go do some push ups to get a better standing in that list.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Without thinking, you let your fist fly and it hits the bag so hard it makes a loud noise as it hits the hole, and the numbers start changing, and you hold your breath until they land on 550 out of 999, putting you at the top of the high score! You jump and bite your lips, in an adorable display of pride. But maybe there’s still some room for improvement?<<else>>Fist. Bag. Impact. The bang is so loud some neighbors get worried, and you fear for the equipment while the numbers start calculating… a perfect 999 out of 999! You massage your hand beaming with pride, wondering what kind of damage you could cause with these fists of steel.<</if>> And back to your apartment you go, to continue with your day.
	<<elseif _posingLevel is 1>>
	You stretch in front of the mirror, and get that itch to check how your posing is going, and get some practice in. Rotating your shoulders, you think it’s time to pull out the big guns, figuratively, as you take your top off to try that front double biceps routine. <<if $muscle < 25>>You will have to settle with your twig arms for now, but that just means there’s more room for improvement. <<elseif $muscle < 35>>You want to take these baby guns out for a ride.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You’ve caught yourself plenty of times checking out your own upper arms, so it’s the perfect opportunity.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Given how much people ask to check out your guns, it just feels right.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Not that you even need to flex in order for people to see how thick your arms have become.<<else>>Given that your biceps are already the size of melons even relaxed, this ought to be good.<</if>> You raise your arms tentatively, after all, flexing your biceps is one of the most culturally celebrated displays of strength - how much training could it possibly require?<br><br> But you did some research, realizing that the angle you bend your elbows and position your fist affects your flex. <<if $muscle < 25>>But even with that knowledge, there are no biceps to show off, making the effort ultimately fruitless.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>That small bump is brought to its best form - which, admittedly, isn’t all that much, but at least you feel like you kind of know what you are doing now.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You tease out your nice and toned biceps, giving your arm that great rounded and aerodynamic shape, which make you proud of yourself.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>And so you summon these great biceps into existence, complete with a nice peak to drive home your progress.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Enormous balls of muscle emerge at your command, complete with veins and clear separation, reminding you how ready you are for a bodybuilding competition in the physique department.<<else>>Your jaw drops as you somehow discover you can make your biceps even bigger through training, the impossible peaked mounds crisscrossed with veins and entire valleys of definition that boggle the mind.<</if>> It’s nice to see you learned the basics of the double biceps pose, but you feel like that is just the beginning of your competitive journey..<br><br> But one cannot do a gun show and not want to show off their strength, and so you get all pumped up (heh) for a little test of your strength. You are then reminded that the landlord installed one of those punching arcade games in the landry, what best way to see how powerful you are than with the speed of your fists?<br><br> You arrive at the empty laundry room, the red tower with a punching bag blinking in silence. You gather some pocket change and get in position, trying to channel all those boxing movies you watched - which, incidentally, reminds you that you have no clue what you are doing. And after inserting the coin, the bag is dropped to its lowered position and the machine starts playing some beepy music. Your eyes lock in on your target, and you wind up, preparing to hit your new inanimate foe. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your hand flies and connects with the bag… with a pitiful whimper as it retracts, and the machine barely registers it, showing a 15 out of 999. You secretly hope there is no low score memory, because you feel embarrassed enough as it is.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>The punch hits with a decent thud, and the three digital numbers start rolling as the machine evaluates your punch. It finally settles on a 70 out of 999, which you somehow hope isn’t as low as it sounds. But you notice the high scores in the 350-450 range, and realize you still got some work ahead of you.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Feeling confident, you pretend to dodge a few imaginary punches before letting your fist fly - it lands with a satisfying thump, and you hear the bag recoiling in its housing as the numbers roll… and give you a 275. Not bad, you are getting closer to the high scores in the 350-450 range. You squeeze your fist, looking at the machine, anxious to get yourself in that scoreboard.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You twist your torso, using all your newfound strength and hit the bag with a loud thud, and it flies back into the slot, causing the digital display to come to life… giving you a 390 out of 999, putting you at the middle of the high score list. You pump your fist with excitement, feeling a sudden urge to go do some push ups to get a better standing in that list.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Without thinking, you let your fist fly and it hits the bag so hard it makes a loud noise as it hits the hole, and the numbers start changing, and you hold your breath until they land on 550 out of 999, putting you at the top of the high score! You jump and bite your lips, in an adorable display of pride. But maybe there’s still some room for improvement?<<else>>Fist. Bag. Impact. The bang is so loud some neighbors get worried, and you fear for the equipment while the numbers start calculating… a perfect 999 out of 999! You massage your hand beaming with pride, wondering what kind of damage you could cause with these fists of steel.<</if>> And back to your apartment you go, to continue with your day.
	<<elseif _posingLevel is 2>>
	You stretch in front of the mirror, and get that itch to check how your posing is going, and get some practice in. Rotating your shoulders, you think it’s time to pull out the big guns, figuratively, as you take your top off to try that front double biceps routine. <<if $muscle < 25>>You will have to settle with your twig arms for now, but that just means there’s more room for improvement. <<elseif $muscle < 35>>You want to take these baby guns out for a ride.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You’ve caught yourself plenty of times checking out your own upper arms, so it’s the perfect opportunity.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Given how much people ask to check out your guns, it just feels right.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Not that you even need to flex in order for people to see how thick your arms have become.<<else>>Given that your biceps are already the size of melons even relaxed, this ought to be good.<</if>> You raise your arms tentatively, after all, flexing your biceps is one of the most culturally celebrated displays of strength - how much training could it possibly require?<br><br> Well, practice makes perfect, and you certainly have put in the effort. Knowing the proper position, you now intend to master the act of slowly engaging your arms as you raise your fists, making the movement smooth and confident. <<if $muscle < 25>>While the move DOES feel trained and practiced, the actual muscle (or lack thereof), does not. So you remind yourself to hit the weights to make the effort count in the future.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>Even if it is a small bump, you somehow manage to get a very dramatic (if modest) rise. It’s a start, but you salivate with the idea of how awesome that would look with a bit more mass.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You get yourself downright horny just watching as the little bundles of muscle slowly reveal themselves, like a magic trick that brings volume and firmness to your arms… with all the panache of a professional magician.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You marvel at the large slabs of meat contracting, the existing volume from your relaxed, thick upper arms slowly coiling themselves into a more defined and peaked version of themselves. It’s almost hypnotic, really.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Truth be told, your strong arms look pretty awesome relaxed as it is, but you have now gotten to the point where the art of flexing them into true mountains of muscle is almost like a seductive dance.<<else>>You lack the words to explain. Even relaxed, your arms are thicker than many men’s legs. But the very act of flexing somehow results in a miraculous display of power as it transmogrifies into this behemoth of veins, definition and peaks.<</if>> It feels like you nailed the art of showing off your biceps. But deep down you realize that is part of the entire pose, and there is still ways to perform a more professional looking pose.<br><br> But one cannot do a gun show and not want to show off their strength, and so you get all pumped up (heh) for a little test of your strength. You are then reminded that the landlord installed one of those punching arcade games in the landry, what best way to see how powerful you are than with the speed of your fists?<br><br> You arrive at the empty laundry room, the red tower with a punching bag blinking in silence. You gather some pocket change and get in position, trying to channel all those boxing movies you watched - which, incidentally, reminds you that you have no clue what you are doing. And after inserting the coin, the bag is dropped to its lowered position and the machine starts playing some beepy music. Your eyes lock in on your target, and you wind up, preparing to hit your new inanimate foe. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your hand flies and connects with the bag… with a pitiful whimper as it retracts, and the machine barely registers it, showing a 15 out of 999. You secretly hope there is no low score memory, because you feel embarrassed enough as it is.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>The punch hits with a decent thud, and the three digital numbers start rolling as the machine evaluates your punch. It finally settles on a 70 out of 999, which you somehow hope isn’t as low as it sounds. But you notice the high scores in the 350-450 range, and realize you still got some work ahead of you.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Feeling confident, you pretend to dodge a few imaginary punches before letting your fist fly - it lands with a satisfying thump, and you hear the bag recoiling in its housing as the numbers roll… and give you a 275. Not bad, you are getting closer to the high scores in the 350-450 range. You squeeze your fist, looking at the machine, anxious to get yourself in that scoreboard.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You twist your torso, using all your newfound strength and hit the bag with a loud thud, and it flies back into the slot, causing the digital display to come to life… giving you a 390 out of 999, putting you at the middle of the high score list. You pump your fist with excitement, feeling a sudden urge to go do some push ups to get a better standing in that list.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Without thinking, you let your fist fly and it hits the bag so hard it makes a loud noise as it hits the hole, and the numbers start changing, and you hold your breath until they land on 550 out of 999, putting you at the top of the high score! You jump and bite your lips, in an adorable display of pride. But maybe there’s still some room for improvement?<<else>>Fist. Bag. Impact. The bang is so loud some neighbors get worried, and you fear for the equipment while the numbers start calculating… a perfect 999 out of 999! You massage your hand beaming with pride, wondering what kind of damage you could cause with these fists of steel.<</if>> And back to your apartment you go, to continue with your day.
