	You stretch in front of the mirror, and get that itch to check how your posing is going, and get some practice in. Rotating your shoulders, you think it’s time to pull out the big guns, figuratively, as you take your top off to try that front double biceps routine. <<if $muscle < 25>>You will have to settle with your twig arms for now, but that just means there’s more room for improvement. <<elseif $muscle < 35>>You want to take these baby guns out for a ride.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You’ve caught yourself plenty of times checking out your own upper arms, so it’s the perfect opportunity.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Given how much people ask to check out your guns, it just feels right.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Not that you even need to flex in order for people to see how thick your arms have become.<<else>>Given that your biceps are already the size of melons even relaxed, this ought to be good.<</if>> You raise your arms tentatively, after all, flexing your biceps is one of the most culturally celebrated displays of strength - how much training could it possibly require?<br><br> At this point? Not much more. You put in the work, and it shows. You watch yourself in the mirror, eyes radiating confidence… with a hint of excitement as you prepare to unleash your perfected double biceps routine. You methodically place your arms, slowly and deliberately, and you prepare your entire body to form a perfect X shape. <<if $muscle < 25>> The execution? Flawless. The physique? Eh, it feels really lopsided, to be sincere. But at least you feel like you got the stage presence down pat.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>The hard work shows, both in your presentation and your burgeoning muscles, which are pushed to their very limit. Unfortunately, while you DO look strong by maximizing what you have, it’s nowhere near the level expected in this kind of competition.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>You almost gasp as you watch that woman in the reflection, the perfect idea of a fitness competition, idealized in every way. You look fierce, with the kind of presence and power that would be at home in the cover of a fantasy book.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>Your honed muscles shine from top to bottom: powerfully muscled shoulders, framed by enviable pumped arms cascade into incredible abs and impressive legs. There is nothing that is not screaming TOP LEVEL PROFESSIONAL BODYBUILDER. It brings a smirk to your face. <<elseif $muscle < 65>>You can barely believe your eyes. You spent hours watching professional male bodybuilders, the best in their field, and frankly? They have nothing on you - from the size of their muscles to their proficiency onstage? You could go next to any of them and not leave anything wanting. You feel completely ready.<<else>>...<br>...<br>...<br>Never have eyes been laid on such a perfect specimen in the history of humanity. You look like an idealized mythological giant, nay, a goddess of bodybuilding who descended from the skies… you are just missing some clouds and rays of sun. You look larger and more powerful than the biggest of bodybuilders in history, with a stage presence that could humble the legends themselves. You stare at perfection, and it stares back at you with unshakable confidence.<</if>> There is no doubt that you have achieved all you possibly could with your posing. You really cannot see much reason to keep trying to improve what cannot get any better.<br><br> But one cannot do a gun show and not want to show off their strength, and so you get all pumped up (heh) for a little test of your strength. You are then reminded that the landlord installed one of those punching arcade games in the landry, what best way to see how powerful you are than with the speed of your fists?<br><br> You arrive at the empty laundry room, the red tower with a punching bag blinking in silence. You gather some pocket change and get in position, trying to channel all those boxing movies you watched - which, incidentally, reminds you that you have no clue what you are doing. And after inserting the coin, the bag is dropped to its lowered position and the machine starts playing some beepy music. Your eyes lock in on your target, and you wind up, preparing to hit your new inanimate foe. <<if $muscle < 25>>Your hand flies and connects with the bag… with a pitiful whimper as it retracts, and the machine barely registers it, showing a 15 out of 999. You secretly hope there is no low score memory, because you feel embarrassed enough as it is.<<elseif $muscle < 35>>The punch hits with a decent thud, and the three digital numbers start rolling as the machine evaluates your punch. It finally settles on a 70 out of 999, which you somehow hope isn’t as low as it sounds. But you notice the high scores in the 350-450 range, and realize you still got some work ahead of you.<<elseif $muscle < 45>>Feeling confident, you pretend to dodge a few imaginary punches before letting your fist fly - it lands with a satisfying thump, and you hear the bag recoiling in its housing as the numbers roll… and give you a 275. Not bad, you are getting closer to the high scores in the 350-450 range. You squeeze your fist, looking at the machine, anxious to get yourself in that scoreboard.<<elseif $muscle < 55>>You twist your torso, using all your newfound strength and hit the bag with a loud thud, and it flies back into the slot, causing the digital display to come to life… giving you a 390 out of 999, putting you at the middle of the high score list. You pump your fist with excitement, feeling a sudden urge to go do some push ups to get a better standing in that list.<<elseif $muscle < 65>>Without thinking, you let your fist fly and it hits the bag so hard it makes a loud noise as it hits the hole, and the numbers start changing, and you hold your breath until they land on 550 out of 999, putting you at the top of the high score! You jump and bite your lips, in an adorable display of pride. But maybe there’s still some room for improvement?<<else>>Fist. Bag. Impact. The bang is so loud some neighbors get worried, and you fear for the equipment while the numbers start calculating… a perfect 999 out of 999! You massage your hand beaming with pride, wondering what kind of damage you could cause with these fists of steel.<</if>> And back to your apartment you go, to continue with your day.
